index 4479b53..aaacab1 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,31 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## WebMCP tools
+
+The application registers browser-native tools through `document.modelContext` on
+all pages using the shared layout. Use a WebMCP-capable browser in a secure context
+(HTTPS or localhost); browsers without the API continue to use the regular UI.
+WebMCP is evolving, so use a browser exposing the current `document.modelContext`
+API described in the [WebMCP imperative API documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api).
+
+| Tool | Input | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `search_articles` | `{ "query": "coffee", "limit": 10 }` | Searches titles and summaries; returns matching metadata, article links and total count. Limit is optional, defaults to 10, and accepts 1–50. |
+| `get_reading_list` | `{}` | Returns articles saved in the current browser session. |
+| `set_article_bookmark` | `{ "slug": "coffee-alchemy", "bookmarked": true }` | Saves the article; use `false` to remove it. Repeated requests preserve the requested state. |
+
+Search and reading-list reads carry `readOnlyHint`. Bookmark updates use the same
+session API and client notifications as the UI, so open reading lists and bookmark
+buttons update immediately. The reading-list endpoint still accepts legacy
+`{ "slug": "..." }` toggle requests, and also supports the explicit `bookmarked`
+boolean used by tools and UI controls. No cross-origin tool exposure is enabled.
+
+Tools validate inputs at runtime and return `{ error: "..." }` for recoverable
+failures. Execution cancellation is passed to network requests. Registration uses
+an `AbortSignal` and is renewed after Astro page transitions; leaving a page also
+cancels its in-flight tool requests. A cancelled write may already have reached
+the server; reading the list again reconciles its state.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for automated tool tests and `pnpm build` for a production build.
